<title>UK: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			14/8/97		  07/8/97	     15/8/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	350-375		  375-400		   450</p>
<p>    Naphtha		50		    50-75		75-100</p>
<p>    Gas oil   1,900-1,950	    1,850-1,900		 1,650</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	275-300			300		   375</p>
<p>    Jet kero	  25-50			 10		 15-20</p>
<p>Gasoline was slightly lower, reflecting outgoing barge movements.</p>
<p>Naphtha was steady with little buying into the German petrochemical industry.</p>
<p>Gas oil was active with incoming Russian cargoes offset by barge sales into Germany, Switzerland and Benelux countries.</p>
<p>Fuel was balanced with incoming material from Germany and outgoing from ARA refineries and bunkering.</p>
<p>Jet stocks rose on demand for blending into the gas oil pool.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5387</p>
</text>
